"Allegretto Account — Quota Bug: \"Login Device\" Calls Classified as \"Model Inference\" - Kimi K2 - Kimi Forum (https://forum.moonshot.ai/t/allegretto-account-quota-bug-login-device-calls-classified-as-model-inference/407)\nciteturn41172search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; Morty May 20, 2026, 5:48am 1\n\n# Allegretto Account — Quota Bug: \"Login Device\" Calls Classified as \"Model Inference\"\n\nDeveloper Support Kimi K2\n\nMorty May 20, 2026, 5:48am 1\n\nMy usage history shows 100+ “Login Device” entries all logged as “Model Inference” calls, consuming my monthly quota. Dashboard shows 15% weekly / 10% monthly remaining, but API returns `429 exceeded_current_quota_error`. I have 3 CLI devices registered. This appears to be a quota classification/tracking bug, not legitimate usage.\n\nyuikns May 21, 2026, 2:35pm 2\n\nTo clarify, the 100+ “Login Device” entries are your actual model inference calls authenticated via device login, not background keep-alive pings.\n\nFor a detailed explanation of this naming convention and the dashboard sync behavior, please see: TITLE : Allegretto Quota System Has Hidden Dual-Pool Architecture + Potential \"Login Device\" Classification Bug - #2 by yuikns--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMoonshot AI · GitHub (https://github.com/MoonshotAI)\nciteturn41172view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/MoonshotAI\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 311\nL0: cite0†Skip to content L1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3: cite1†Sign in L4: \nL5: Appearance settings\nL6: \nL7: cite2†MoonshotAI L8: \nL9:   * Platform\nL10: \nL11:     * AI CODE CREATION\nL12:       * cite3†GitHub CopilotWrite better code with AI L13:       * cite4†GitHub Copilot appDirect agents from issue to merge L14:       * cite5†MCP RegistryIntegrate external tools L15:     * DEVELOPER WORKFLOWS\nL16:       * cit